    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are operating with a thin slate today as we navigate the final stretch of the 2026 season. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** both sidelined by schedule gaps, the offensive burden shifts to our remaining depth. **Brayan Rocchio** occupies the only active starting slot, holding a marginal 43.06 score against Freddy Peralta. While his base projection is solid, the combination of a pending lineup status\u2014likely forcing him into the bottom of the order\u2014and Peralta\u2019s respectable 4.32 xERA suppresses his upside. We are prioritizing his floor here, but given his sprint speed profile and ability to navigate high-leverage situations, he remains our sole focus for securing a potential stolen base contribution.\n\nThe most challenging decision for today\u2019s lineup was keeping **Liam Hicks** on the bench with a 33.31 score. Despite a favorable potential #4 spot in the order, the optimizer penalized **Liam Hicks** due to the tough matchup against Parker Messick. Facing a left-handed arm with a 3.51 xERA significantly degraded **Liam Hicks**\u2019 platoon efficiency, effectively capping his potential in this specific park environment. While **Luis Robert Jr.** remains held out on the IL, we continue to monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Heliot Ramos** for future rotations. With the current absence of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Jacob Wilson**, we are playing conservatively, preserving our remaining daily games by benching fringe options like **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Coby Mayo** until we face more favorable pitching conditions.",
